1
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:16,060
One day Suzie McCash went shopping with her mum in Tynemouth, England.

2
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:19,215
Suzie was four years old.

3
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:24,915
Her mum didn’t feel very well at the shops, so they went home.

4
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:29,720
In the house, Suzie’s mum went to lie on the sofa.

5
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:32,480
She was there for a long time.

6
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:37,500
Her eyes were shut and it wasn’t easy for her to breathe.

7
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:39,560
Suzie was worried.

8
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:42,140
Was her mum really ill?

9
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:48,054
Suzie went to the house next door, but the neighbours weren’t there.

10
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:54,962
So she phoned 999 – the emergency telephone number for the police.

11
00:00:55,620 --> 00:01:00,651
The police officer was very kind and Suzie was calm.

12
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:03,860
‘What’s your mummy doing now?’

13
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:09,600
‘Um, she’s just sitting on the sofa and she’s doing nothing.’

14
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:12,120
‘Are her eyes open?’

15
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:14,560
‘No, they’re shut.’

16
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:16,560
And later…

17
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:18,739
‘Can you open the door?

18
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:20,940
Can you be a big girl?’

19
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:27,144
Soon the police were at their house and an ambulance was there, too.

20
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:31,800
About an hour later, Suzie’s mum was OK again.

21
00:01:32,520 --> 00:01:36,177
A doctor said: ‘Her mummy was very sick.

22
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:40,357
Without Suzie’s phone call, her mummy might be dead now.’

23
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:46,980
Suzie’s story was in the newspapers and people were surprised and happy about it.

24
00:01:47,600 --> 00:02:00,380
She was a very brave girl and, a year later, she was in the news again because she was named a Child of Courage at the Pride of Britain Awards for helping her mother.
